Translation patch: spqr::initial_state

Change:
1. the `log::info!` call is commented out;
2. `PqRatchetState { .. }.encode_to_vec()` becomes `encode_state_pb(&PqRatchetState { .. })`.
Why:
1. `log` is excluded from the translation; its macros make Aeneas fail ("Internal error");
2. `encode_state_pb` is opaque in the translation, so the prost-derived `Message` impls are not
   reached (#102, aeneas#1046).
Behaviour: identical apart from logging (no log output).
Relies on: `encode_state_pb`, added by lib-state_pb.patch.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 6bc0197..05daed8 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -209,27 +209,26 @@ fn init_inner(v: Version, d: Direction, auth_key: &[u8]) -> Option<pqrpb::pq_rat
 }
 
 pub fn initial_state(params: Params) -> Result<SerializedState, Error> {
-    #[cfg(not(hax))]
-    log::info!(
-        "spqr initiating state with version {:?} and direction {:?}",
-        params.version,
-        params.direction
-    );
+    // #[cfg(not(hax))]
+    // log::info!(
